WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.900
Note: Frenzy Diary

00:00.390 --> 00:02.760
August 2nd. The universal honeymoon date.

00:02.760 --> 00:05.470
Me and my darling finally went off to our long awaited honeymoon!

00:05.470 --> 00:10.190
However, the plane that took flight with hopes and dreams got shot down by a UMA.

00:10.190 --> 00:14.970
On a lone, uninhabited island, we're saved by a kind boy, Pierre, but enjoyed only a moment of peace.

00:14.970 --> 00:17.780
Now Yuuka's been kidnapped by an army of huge monkeys!

00:17.780 --> 00:21.750
Um, Kyouka, there's a discrepancy with the facts I'm aware of.

00:21.750 --> 00:23.870
Our cute daughter is in a castle in the sky.

00:23.870 --> 00:26.170
A strange old man has appeared in front of her.

00:26.170 --> 00:27.950
How will this development end?

00:27.950 --> 00:29.420
Ready, start!

01:51.150 --> 01:52.640
The party will start soon.

01:52.640 --> 01:55.210
It's a wonderful party, therefore it'll be pointless if you don't watch it.

01:55.210 --> 01:58.010
So pigs, let's get this started, shall we?

02:21.990 --> 02:23.870
I am absolutely not a monkey!

02:23.870 --> 02:27.110
Biologically, there are barriers that humans and monkeys cannot overcome!

02:27.110 --> 02:30.920
And yet, to call me a monkey when I am a human just because I resemble a monkey!

02:29.620 --> 02:31.960
Um, Oji-san?

02:36.290 --> 02:37.840
G-Gekka!

02:37.840 --> 02:38.880
O-Oji-san!

02:39.970 --> 02:41.510
Oji-san, are you all right?

02:42.110 --> 02:44.350
I do not prefer such a fuss.

02:44.350 --> 02:46.160
What? Who was that?

02:48.140 --> 02:49.840
Wow, he's still alive.

02:49.840 --> 02:51.360
I'm simply happy for you.

02:51.360 --> 02:55.980
I'm simply a bad girl for calling you a monkey.

02:56.400 --> 02:57.580
I'm sorry.

02:59.120 --> 03:02.280
I look like a human to you?

03:02.280 --> 03:04.320
You are a human, right?

03:04.320 --> 03:06.790
What? Wait? You are a human, right?

03:09.580 --> 03:12.050
I will pledge my loyalty to you.

03:12.050 --> 03:14.540
Thank you for acknowledging me as a human!

03:14.720 --> 03:17.550
I'm a scientist named Saruwatari Inuhiko.

03:17.550 --> 03:18.710
Saruwatari...

03:18.960 --> 03:20.050
Inuhiko?

03:20.590 --> 03:21.860
A scientist?

03:22.250 --> 03:23.550
Saruwatari?

03:24.680 --> 03:26.860
Is there something, Hyouka?

03:26.860 --> 03:28.660
Oh no, nothing.

03:28.660 --> 03:32.040
I've had a weak health since I was little.

03:32.040 --> 03:33.890
And this face.

03:33.890 --> 03:36.590
Everyone made fun of me and never treated me like a human.

03:36.590 --> 03:39.560
I was always facing a sense of inferiority.

03:40.110 --> 03:42.570
Yes, experiences like that hurt.

03:42.570 --> 03:45.450
But I hate losing.

03:45.450 --> 03:48.620
So I decided to surprise the world with something else.

03:48.620 --> 03:50.580
Yes, with this.

03:50.920 --> 03:54.560
The more people made fun of me, the more I studied.

03:54.560 --> 03:59.020
Eventually, I gained the position as a leading researcher of artificial life forms,

03:59.020 --> 04:02.470
and I won against all those who made fun of me.

04:02.470 --> 04:04.220
Artificial life forms?

04:04.220 --> 04:08.470
I wanted to create a life that would listen to anything I said.

04:08.470 --> 04:11.140
A doll that would move as I told it to.

04:11.520 --> 04:12.770
A doll...

04:12.770 --> 04:19.100
But unfortunately, a huge problem developed with the team I was working with at the time.

04:19.660 --> 04:23.650
With all hope lost, I wandered around, avoiding people's eyes,

04:23.650 --> 04:25.660
and eventually made it to this island.

04:25.660 --> 04:29.400
I didn't want to talk to anyone nor see anyone.

04:29.400 --> 04:34.890
I hid myself in this floating castle and swore never to return to the world.

04:35.620 --> 04:38.170
Yes, that's what I swore...

04:42.840 --> 04:44.400
Oji-sama?

04:44.400 --> 04:48.460
But it seems humans can't live alone.

04:48.460 --> 04:50.710
Being as weak a person as I am, I became lonely soon enough,

04:50.710 --> 04:57.400
so I used the remains of the Areato, the natives of this island, to resume my research on artificial life.

04:57.730 --> 05:02.360
But it's no good! A failure! A failure! A failure! All a failure!

05:03.040 --> 05:05.860
I tried to make a human.

05:05.860 --> 05:07.160
Yet!

05:07.360 --> 05:08.240
Monkeys!

05:08.340 --> 05:09.460
Monkeys!

05:09.460 --> 05:12.830
No matter how many I make,
they always turn into monkeys!

05:12.990 --> 05:16.470
Freaky monkeys like those won't soothe me!

05:16.470 --> 05:18.280
They won't love me!

05:18.280 --> 05:21.340
Oh, monkeys... Am I being cursed by monkeys?

05:21.340 --> 05:23.740
U-Um, Oji-sama, please calm down.

05:23.740 --> 05:25.250
I'm a human.

05:25.250 --> 05:27.230
I wanted a human to love me!

05:28.890 --> 05:29.850
Oji-sama!

05:31.420 --> 05:33.430
Hey, here's a human.

05:34.890 --> 05:37.160
I don't have much life left in me.

05:37.160 --> 05:42.150
I wish I could end my life being watched over by a cute girl like you.

05:44.990 --> 05:45.940
Gekka!

05:48.620 --> 05:53.740
So, little girl. You will become an obedient doll for this poor old man, won't you?

05:54.390 --> 05:56.370
Mom, help me!

06:02.630 --> 06:03.650
Kitty!

06:03.650 --> 06:04.380
Are you all right?

06:04.710 --> 06:05.630
Kyouka?

06:07.830 --> 06:08.940
This is great!

06:08.940 --> 06:10.890
The bug's done it!

06:10.890 --> 06:13.140
Show a little mercy, and he takes it too far!

06:13.890 --> 06:15.600
What exactly happened?

06:15.600 --> 06:17.240
What happened to Yuuka?

06:17.240 --> 06:20.170
There's no time for explanations! Yuuka is in danger!

06:20.170 --> 06:21.680
I'll kill that rotten professor!

06:21.080 --> 06:22.400
Calm down, Kyouka.

06:23.080 --> 06:25.780
If it means saving Yuuka, I will lend a hand.

06:26.440 --> 06:29.400
So you can go into a frenzy if it's for the family?

06:30.970 --> 06:32.030
Naturally.

06:32.030 --> 06:33.100
Me, too.

06:33.100 --> 06:36.340
I'm the one most worried about Yuuka-chan, after all.

06:36.340 --> 06:37.470
Likewise for me.

06:37.470 --> 06:38.610
And me, too.

06:38.610 --> 06:41.080
I'd do anything for Yuuka-chan.

06:41.410 --> 06:43.980
Um, allow me to give my support, too.

06:43.980 --> 06:46.090
So everyone likes Yuuka.

06:46.640 --> 06:47.620
I like her, too.

06:47.620 --> 06:49.160
She's so transparent and honest.

06:49.160 --> 06:53.970
She lived a life longer and harsher than me,
yet she always smiles kindly.

06:54.380 --> 06:56.330
So I will protect Yuuka.

06:56.330 --> 06:58.260
I cannot forgive anyone that does harm to her.

06:58.260 --> 07:01.350
Although, I don't know what a biological weapon can do.

07:01.710 --> 07:05.860
Yes, very good. You pigs are thinking about what you can do with the brains you're given.

07:06.320 --> 07:11.820
Very well. I just came up with an amazing party that will leave no mark in the end after hearing all your words!

07:11.980 --> 07:12.860
"Party"?

07:13.100 --> 07:15.740
Our enemy is a rotting professor and stupid white monkeys!

07:15.740 --> 07:18.560
Our goal is the retrieval of Yuuka and Gekka,
and retaliation against them!

07:18.560 --> 07:19.490
I call this:

07:19.490 --> 07:21.820
"Charming! Apron Dress and Delicious Food."

07:21.820 --> 07:24.520
"Operation Feed the Scum Bags!!"

07:24.520 --> 07:26.380
It sounds really fishy.

07:28.820 --> 07:31.130
My dream will finally come true.

07:31.130 --> 07:35.070
I will be watched over by a human as a human and end my life as a human.

07:36.090 --> 07:37.640
The angel has finally come to me.

07:37.640 --> 07:40.210
I will not let go of her.

07:40.560 --> 07:44.770
Stall those who try to take my angel back.

07:48.540 --> 07:50.740
Hi, welcome!

07:50.740 --> 07:52.530
The big party, this way please.

07:52.530 --> 07:53.530
Come on in.

07:53.840 --> 07:57.030
Welcome to the Riverside Outdoor Stand.

07:57.380 --> 07:59.520
You are all very lucky.

07:59.520 --> 08:01.690
Today's the first day of the event, so we won't ask for money.

08:01.690 --> 08:04.420
Please eat all you want and enjoy yourselves

08:04.420 --> 08:06.140
Now let me introduce you.

08:06.140 --> 08:08.960
Your cook of the night is your hotel's proud five-star chef,

08:08.960 --> 08:11.740
Pierre Nishikura!

08:11.740 --> 08:12.720
Hello.

08:12.720 --> 08:16.600
And the ones making your night an exciting one are these folks, who came all the way from the Great Japanese Empire,

08:16.600 --> 08:18.640
the Show Dancers!

08:24.180 --> 08:25.610
I did have a bad feeling about this.

08:25.610 --> 08:30.110
I'm the last of the Bister King's bloodline, and yet I'm...

08:30.110 --> 08:32.530
Yay! Everyone enjoying themselves?!

08:32.530 --> 08:35.690
Welcome back, Masters.

08:37.320 --> 08:39.830
Please, everyone. Don't just stand there.

08:40.060 --> 08:41.560
Take your seats.

09:03.240 --> 09:06.490
No need to rush. There's plenty to go around.

09:06.490 --> 09:10.820
Hey, Pierre! Your food's getting great feedback!

09:08.930 --> 09:10.820
Thank you very much.

09:11.040 --> 09:14.940
You're free to go cuddle with your mascot character, Teika-kun.

09:14.940 --> 09:16.530
Come on over, kids!

09:19.880 --> 09:22.330
This humiliation. I think I'll puke blood.

09:22.730 --> 09:24.960
You can, but don't show it to our guests.

09:24.960 --> 09:27.300
We're on a roll, too!

09:27.300 --> 09:29.330
Everyone, clapping please.

09:31.800 --> 09:33.300
This is great.

09:37.120 --> 09:39.180
But why are we doing this?

09:39.180 --> 09:40.760
Continue, Father.

09:40.760 --> 09:42.560
Hyouka. But...

09:42.950 --> 09:45.230
I'm sure Mother has a plan.

09:45.230 --> 09:46.980
This is all to save Yuuka.

09:46.980 --> 09:47.830
So...

09:52.390 --> 09:54.760
Fine! I'll go all the way!

09:59.360 --> 10:00.860
They're all monkeys, after all.

10:00.860 --> 10:05.960
But this looks like we're only feeding the monkeys.

10:05.960 --> 10:08.640
That's what makes you an amateur.

10:08.640 --> 10:09.650
Watch.

10:09.650 --> 10:12.290
Attention please, everyone!

10:12.290 --> 10:15.920
We, the staff, are very happy to see your reactions.

10:15.920 --> 10:19.340
However, are you all really satisfied with the food you see?

10:19.340 --> 10:22.970
Wouldn't you want to eat something that's even tastier?

10:22.970 --> 10:26.250
Hey, I bet you all thought,
"There can't be anything like that," didn't you?

10:26.250 --> 10:27.770
It turns out there is!

10:30.350 --> 10:33.650
However, there is a limitation to that food.

10:33.650 --> 10:38.070
So we will specially serve it to those who give us what we're after.

10:40.730 --> 10:41.880
The item is...

10:41.880 --> 10:42.700
This!

10:46.940 --> 10:49.520
Yes. I'm sure you've seen this somewhere before.

10:49.520 --> 10:53.540
The price we ask is this glowing blue stone.

11:09.520 --> 11:12.270
Do I have to return to what I was?

11:12.270 --> 11:14.770
To a doll that listens obediently to someone?

11:14.960 --> 11:16.850
But I don't want that.

11:16.850 --> 11:19.690
I thought I was finally able to become a person.

11:20.190 --> 11:22.490
Dad! Mom!

11:26.450 --> 11:28.310
No! No!

11:32.310 --> 11:33.740
Monkeys?

11:39.250 --> 11:40.480
Don't worry.

11:42.760 --> 11:43.930
It's me.

11:45.530 --> 11:46.510
Hyouka.

11:47.290 --> 11:48.770
I was so scared.

11:49.160 --> 11:50.020
Don't move.

11:59.500 --> 12:00.740
What's going on?

12:02.210 --> 12:03.570
Yes, I did it!

12:03.730 --> 12:05.130
The castle in the sky is...

12:05.130 --> 12:06.930
How is this happening?

12:06.930 --> 12:08.280
It's simple.

12:08.280 --> 12:12.620
I fed the monkeys for free with food that they had never tasted before.

12:12.700 --> 12:15.960
Because of that, they lost control, and they obeyed me.

12:15.960 --> 12:19.340
They flew back hearing there was even better food.

12:19.340 --> 12:23.220
Yes, to bring this back to me as the price for the food.

12:23.220 --> 12:24.550
Th-That's!

12:24.550 --> 12:28.390
Looks like monkeys were also vulnerable to the word "limited".

12:28.390 --> 12:34.110
They fought over the levistones,
and the castle lost the force to keep it up.

12:34.110 --> 12:39.360
All that's left is for us to wait for Hyouka, who followed the monkeys as they flew back, to save Yuuka.

12:38.260 --> 12:40.310
I see the story now.

12:40.310 --> 12:45.170
So you weren't just feeding the monkey Pierre-san's food for nothing.

12:45.500 --> 12:46.610
Yuuka...

12:47.780 --> 12:49.620
Watch out, Yuuka.

12:50.100 --> 12:50.850
Yeah.

12:52.840 --> 12:54.900
Th-The monkeys!

12:57.630 --> 13:00.540
You shouldn't. You can tell the difference in strength, right?

13:00.540 --> 13:02.560
But I don't care if you want to die.

13:03.090 --> 13:04.590
I will kill you painlessly.

13:05.970 --> 13:06.970
You can't, Hyouka.

13:07.220 --> 13:09.220
Please don't kill the monkeys!

13:09.860 --> 13:10.740
Why?

13:10.740 --> 13:12.600
Don't you want to leave here?

13:12.970 --> 13:14.810
No, that's not what I mean.

13:14.810 --> 13:18.770
These monkeys haven't done anything bad to me.

13:18.770 --> 13:19.860
So please!

13:23.590 --> 13:25.280
Hang on tight.

13:30.520 --> 13:31.810
Hyouka.

13:31.810 --> 13:33.660
Simply thank you.

13:33.660 --> 13:37.820
If the world had been divided into three,
it would have been Heaven, Hell, and me.

13:38.440 --> 13:44.050
I'm a devil meant to fight for the good of the majority.

13:44.050 --> 13:48.400
In the end, I destroyed the lab and fled before fighting the enemy.

13:48.400 --> 13:51.850
But I can't go to Heaven in this body.

13:51.850 --> 13:56.140
If the world had been divided into three,
it would have been Heaven, Hell, and me.

13:56.140 --> 13:57.120
Hyouka...

13:57.120 --> 14:03.730
Me, too. Born to the Himemiya,
I was never blessed with any care or love.

14:03.730 --> 14:07.860
But I didn't have the courage to make myself become an Oni, so I always did things half-heartedly.

14:07.860 --> 14:10.280
So I can simply understand your feelings.

14:10.750 --> 14:14.870
I don't know what god out there set our fates,

14:14.870 --> 14:21.080
but all of us in the Family Frenzy are half-hearted and can't go to Heaven or Hell.

14:21.930 --> 14:24.550
We were all searching for a family.

14:24.550 --> 14:25.850
Family...

14:25.850 --> 14:27.630
Yeah, I agree.

14:27.630 --> 14:32.550
The greatest mistake in creating me was giving me a heart.

14:32.550 --> 14:36.050
A coward like me would have been useless on the battlefield.

14:36.050 --> 14:38.560
You hurt my ears, Black Thirteen.

14:39.640 --> 14:42.310
I didn't expect us to meet again.

14:42.310 --> 14:44.820
So you were still alive, Professor Saruwatari.

14:46.070 --> 14:50.300
Looks like you're having a pretty entertaining life, Black Thirteen.

14:50.300 --> 14:53.080
Or, should I call you Robes like I used to?

14:53.080 --> 14:54.010
Robes?

14:54.010 --> 14:55.830
Was I ever called like that?

14:57.250 --> 14:58.800
Black Thirteen?

14:58.800 --> 14:59.750
Robes?

14:59.750 --> 15:02.780
Oh, I didn't tell you?

15:02.780 --> 15:07.680
When I was part of the artificial life form project,

15:07.680 --> 15:11.910
the best work created then was the slaughtering biological weapon that stands there,

15:11.910 --> 15:13.800
Black Thirteen.

15:16.020 --> 15:18.520
Then you created Hyouka?

15:18.750 --> 15:23.860
If the project had succeeded, my status as a scientist would have been set.

15:23.860 --> 15:24.980
Yet...

15:32.820 --> 15:37.290
He suddenly went berserk and killed Dr. Gebok, the chief of the group.

15:38.330 --> 15:42.170
Destroyed the lab and disappeared.

15:42.170 --> 15:43.510
Hyouka did that?

15:43.510 --> 15:46.170
Then the "big trouble" you said is...

15:46.170 --> 15:48.750
Thanks to all that happened, here I am.

15:48.750 --> 15:51.170
Robes, would you have any clue?

15:51.170 --> 15:53.870
To have been abandoned by you, to whom I devoted everything,

15:53.870 --> 15:58.550
and then having to hide on this island alone after falling to the pits of despair?

15:58.550 --> 15:59.870
And yet you're...

15:59.870 --> 16:01.890
I'm jealous of you.

16:01.890 --> 16:04.660
If possible, I wanted to be addressed by a name, too.

16:04.660 --> 16:06.160
I wanted to be loved by humans.

16:07.910 --> 16:09.130
Oji-sama!

16:09.130 --> 16:10.030
Professor...

16:10.820 --> 16:17.820
Are you saying that having to be born, to live, and to die here like a monkey is my destiny?!

16:18.280 --> 16:20.580
Without anyone ever loving me...

16:20.580 --> 16:22.750
I get it! Oji-sama is...

16:22.750 --> 16:25.710
But I won't let it end that way.

16:29.810 --> 16:31.140
Monkeys?

16:31.140 --> 16:34.180
These monkeys move as I command them to.

16:34.180 --> 16:36.010
What will you do, Robes?

16:36.010 --> 16:39.920
Will you listen to the angel's words and be reduced to scrap without a fight?

16:39.920 --> 16:41.280
Or...

16:41.920 --> 16:43.020
You can't, Hyouka!

16:43.020 --> 16:45.000
I don't care which.

16:45.000 --> 16:47.980
After all, I have plenty of replacements for these monkeys.

16:47.980 --> 16:50.130
I don't care what happens to you guys.

16:50.130 --> 16:53.150
Bring that girl back to me!

16:54.500 --> 16:56.160
Th-That's so...

16:59.050 --> 17:00.490
That's so mean.

17:00.780 --> 17:02.110
So mean.

17:02.110 --> 17:05.110
Oji-sama... Oji-sama, you idiot!

17:06.140 --> 17:06.990
Yuuka?

17:07.660 --> 17:10.950
No! No! No! You're wrong!

17:10.950 --> 17:13.230
Why don't you see it?

17:13.230 --> 17:14.920
Why do you take it wrong?

17:15.430 --> 17:17.180
You're not alone!

17:17.680 --> 17:19.430
You've had them with you all along!

17:19.430 --> 17:22.570
Those who find you important!

17:22.570 --> 17:23.400
Me?

17:23.400 --> 17:24.960
Where?

17:24.960 --> 17:26.810
Where do you say they are?

17:26.810 --> 17:28.190
The monkeys!

17:28.390 --> 17:30.190
Monkeys, you say?

17:30.500 --> 17:34.620
Yes! These monkeys are actually very kind!

17:34.620 --> 17:36.200
Kind? Them?

17:36.200 --> 17:42.140
The reason why they kidnapped me was because they wanted you to love them back.

17:42.140 --> 17:48.710
They knew you were lonely, but that they couldn't be the ones to ease your loneliness, so they kidnapped me.

17:48.710 --> 17:52.210
And yet you say you don't care what happens to the monkeys?

17:52.700 --> 17:56.340
Why don't you see how the monkeys feel?

17:56.340 --> 18:01.440
You're giving the same pain you felt from people around you to the monkeys.

18:04.010 --> 18:05.390
Y-You guys...

18:06.640 --> 18:08.190
Our King.

18:08.190 --> 18:09.820
Our God.

18:09.820 --> 18:12.110
Everything is for our great lord.

18:12.280 --> 18:13.380
You guys...

18:13.380 --> 18:16.090
You take someone like me as your lord?

18:16.090 --> 18:17.610
You see me as a human?

18:20.260 --> 18:23.600
I see. I see it.

18:24.070 --> 18:25.780
A monkey was fine.

18:25.780 --> 18:28.120
I was fine being a monkey all along.

18:29.620 --> 18:31.640
You're blessed, Oji-sama.

18:31.640 --> 18:33.660
You're cared for by so many.

18:35.790 --> 18:38.240
Are you really an angel?

18:38.880 --> 18:40.020
Hey, Professor.

18:40.020 --> 18:41.570
I can say this now.

18:41.570 --> 18:45.000
I'm glad from the bottom of my heart that I was born.

18:45.000 --> 18:47.140
Thank you for creating me,

18:47.700 --> 18:48.940
Dad.

19:00.560 --> 19:02.030
Oji-sama.

19:02.030 --> 19:03.600
Don't cry, Yuuka.

19:03.600 --> 19:06.800
We should return to our family.

19:07.230 --> 19:07.910
Look.

19:11.490 --> 19:12.720
Yuuka!

19:12.720 --> 19:14.540
I'm glad you're safe.

19:14.540 --> 19:16.430
Dad! Mom!

19:16.430 --> 19:18.670
Nee-sama! Ginka-san! Teika-kun!

19:25.090 --> 19:26.140
Yuuka-chan!

19:28.140 --> 19:31.940
If you can't go frenzy when a family member is in danger, then you're no human!

19:35.950 --> 19:39.690
Yuukaaaaaaa!

19:44.740 --> 19:46.410
What are you doing, Father?

19:46.410 --> 19:48.810
Well, I was, well...

19:48.810 --> 19:49.850
Dad!

19:50.420 --> 19:51.510
Whee!

19:51.980 --> 19:53.100
Yuuka.

19:53.100 --> 19:53.880
Welcome back.

19:53.880 --> 19:55.650
Yup, I'm back.

19:56.500 --> 19:58.770
Ahh, what are they doing?

19:58.770 --> 20:01.840
Hyouka was with her, so that was nothing.

20:02.700 --> 20:04.950
Looks like he lost his cool to the sense of emergency.

20:04.950 --> 20:06.190
Not too bad.

20:06.190 --> 20:07.320
"Not too bad"?

20:09.950 --> 20:11.690
What's going on there?

20:12.420 --> 20:17.320
I see. Looks like they know exactly who was the one serving them the good food.

20:17.320 --> 20:21.280
This is perfect. Pierre! You should become those monkeys' new king starting today!

20:21.280 --> 20:25.660
King?! What are you talking about? That's impossible!

20:25.660 --> 20:26.620
Impossible?

20:26.620 --> 20:28.630
Don't you know the legend of kings being crowned by a god?

20:28.630 --> 20:30.890
The throne of the king is always given by a god!

20:30.890 --> 20:35.260
Even if you return to the Great Japanese Emipre, you'd end your life as nothing more than one of the lowest ranked.

20:35.260 --> 20:37.840
So live here and be like a man as the king of a country!

20:37.840 --> 20:40.480
As a god, I make a declaration.

20:40.480 --> 20:42.480
Pierre is king! The monkeys are citizens!

20:42.480 --> 20:44.460
This is the Independent People's Republic of Kyouka!

20:44.460 --> 20:46.690
You guys come up with your own laws!

20:46.690 --> 20:47.960
Make them come up with it?

20:47.960 --> 20:49.740
Are you sure, Mother?

20:50.070 --> 20:52.600
I said it's okay, so it's okay.

20:52.600 --> 20:54.470
Everything is now solved.

20:54.470 --> 20:56.440
We should start heading home.

20:56.440 --> 20:57.770
But how?

20:57.770 --> 20:58.610
Ah, right.

21:02.620 --> 21:04.850
You guys are cruel.

21:04.850 --> 21:08.870
You left without saving me from that crumbling castle in the sky.

21:09.400 --> 21:11.050
From the castle in the sky?

21:11.050 --> 21:11.790
Who are you?

21:11.790 --> 21:16.000
I guess I'll forgive you, if you will let me eat all the sushi I want.

21:16.000 --> 21:16.790
No, you aren't...

21:16.790 --> 21:18.960
Just a midsummer night's dream.

21:18.960 --> 21:21.410
You'll forget it all once you wake up.

21:21.410 --> 21:25.170
Who I am, or how you made it home.

21:26.500 --> 21:27.920
What is this?

21:33.330 --> 21:34.210
Where am I?

21:34.210 --> 21:35.120
What?

21:35.120 --> 21:37.340
When did we make it home?

21:37.820 --> 21:41.090
We made it back fine, so let's forget about the details.

21:41.090 --> 21:42.170
You think so?

21:42.170 --> 21:46.930
All in all, it was a fun trip, but our home's best, after all.

21:46.930 --> 21:50.390
Kyouka, you didn't plan this just to say that line, did you?

21:50.390 --> 21:52.790
Forget it! Food! Let's have food!

21:52.790 --> 21:56.270
I agree. And for some reason, I really want to eat some sushi tonight.

21:56.270 --> 21:58.220
I'll simply help, too.

21:58.220 --> 21:59.180
Right, Hyouka?

21:59.180 --> 22:01.000
What? Sure.

23:40.770 --> 23:41.840
This is Yuuka.

23:41.840 --> 23:45.100
Eating food with everyone tastes really good.

23:45.100 --> 23:47.860
But I'm so full, I can't eat another bite.

23:48.770 --> 23:51.890
Next time, Kyouran Kazoku Nikki Extra.

23:51.890 --> 23:54.060
Xie Xie. Assassination Chinese.
